INFO  [Claude Code] 2. Issue 2: Test creation for `PubSubConfig.tradePublisher()` - Fixed by the same correction
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] The key problem was that the base class wasn't compiling because the method signatures didn't match the interface requirements (missing `throws PubSubException` declarations).
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] Now let me provide a summary to the user:
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] ## Summary
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] I've identified and resolved the root cause of both Diffblue Cover issues related to `PubSubConfig` test generation.
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] ### Problem Identified
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] The `PubSubConfigDiffblueBase` custom base class that was previously created had a **compilation error** that prevented it from being used by Diffblue Cover:
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] - The stub implementations of `Publisher` and `Subscriber` interfaces were missing required `throws PubSubException` declarations
INFO  [Claude Code] - Since the base class couldn't compile, it wasn't available on the classpath for Diffblue Cover to use
INFO  [Claude Code] - This caused Diffblue to fall back to generating test classes with `@MockBean`, which triggered the bean ambiguity error
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] ### Solution Applied
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] I've updated `/home/jbergqvist/diffblue/finos-traderX/trade-processor/src/test/java/finos/traderx/tradeprocessor/PubSubConfigDiffblueBase.java` to add `throws finos.traderx.messaging.PubSubException` declarations to all methods that require them:
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] - `Publisher.publish()` methods
INFO  [Claude Code] - `Publisher.connect()` and `disconnect()`  
INFO  [Claude Code] - `Subscriber.subscribe()` and `unsubscribe()`
INFO  [Claude Code] - `Subscriber.connect()` and `disconnect()`
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] ### Next Steps
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] **You must compile the test classes** for Diffblue Cover to detect the base class:
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] ```bash
INFO  [Claude Code] ./compile-tests.sh
INFO  [Claude Code] ```
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] Or directly with Gradle:
